„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ,for there is no respect of persons with God.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book,§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡For as many as have sinned without law shall also perish without law: and as many as have sinned in the law shall be judged by the law;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙa(for not the hearers of the law are just before God, but the doers of the law shall be justified.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book,§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ’For when the Gentiles, which have not the law, do by nature the things contained in the law, these, having not the law, are a law unto themselves:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¨which shew the work of the law written in their hearts, their conscience also bearing witness, and their thoughts the mean while accusing or else excusing one another;)¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙZin the day when God shall judge the secrets of men by Jesus Christ according to my gospel.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book,§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSBehold, thou art called a Jew, and restest in the law, and makest thy boast of God,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙhand knowest his will, and approvest the things that are more excellent, being instructed out of the law;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙdand art confident that thou thyself art a guide of the blind, a light of them which are in darkness,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙoan instructor of the foolish, a teacher of babes, which hast the form of knowledge and of the truth in the law.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book,§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ~Thou therefore which teachest another, teachest thou not thyself? thou that preachest a man should not steal, dost thou steal?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„Thou that sayest a man should not commit adultery, dost thou commit adultery? thou that abhorrest idols, dost thou commit sacrilege?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙVThou that makest thy boast of the law, through breaking the law dishonourest thou God?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSFor the name of God is blasphemed among the Gentiles through you, as it is written.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book,§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ†For circumcision verily profiteth, if thou keep the law: but if thou be a breaker of the law, thy circumcision is made uncircumcision.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|Therefore if the uncircumcision keep the righteousness of the law, shall not his uncircumcision be counted for circumcision?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd shall not uncircumcision which is by nature, if it fulfil the law, judge thee, who by the letter and circumcision dost transgress the law?¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book,§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙiFor he is not a Jew, which is one outwardly; neither is that circumcision, which is outward in the flesh:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙœbut he is a Jew, which is one inwardly; and circumcision is that of the heart, in the spirit, and not in the letter; whose praise is not of men, but of God.¦layout ªlast_verse